      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFirst slice of #61024's \"Migrate speculative model code to Flat Model\" bullet (RFC #44219). Moves the Medusa draft-model implementation from the legacy `vllm/model_executor/models/` layout into the new `vllm/models/<name>/<hw>/` layout.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Moves `vllm/model_executor/models/medusa.py` to `vllm/models/medusa/common/medusa.py` + a package `__init__.py`, and repoints the `MedusaModel` entry in `registry.py` to `vllm.models.medusa`.\n- No logic change. The only diff inside the moved file is fixing `from .utils import maybe_prefix` to the now-external `from vllm.model_executor.models.utils import maybe_prefix` (verified by diffing old vs. new file content).\n- Medusa needs only a `common/` directory, no `nvidia`/`amd`/`cpu`/`xpu` split: it's pure `torch.nn` (`Linear`, `SiLU`, `LogitsProcessor`, `ParallelLMHead`), no custom kernels, and has no dependency on any base model's architecture code (unlike e.g. `llama_eagle.py`, which imports `LlamaForCausalLM` directly and so can't move independently of a Llama migration). That made it the first candidate out of the ~30 remaining legacy drafter files.\n\n## Validation\n\n```\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/models/test_registry.py -q -k MedusaModel\n# 1 passed\n\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/config/test_model_arch_config.py -q -k medusa\n# 1 passed\n\npre-commit run --files vllm/model_executor/models/registry.py vllm/models/medusa/__init__.py vllm/models/medusa/common/__init__.py vllm/models/medusa/common/medusa.py\n# all hooks passed (ruff check/format, mypy, SPDX headers, etc.)\n```\n\n**Not yet validated:** `tests/v1/e2e/spec_decode/acceptance_rates/mtp_other/test_medusa.py` (the real `vicuna-7b` + `FasterDecoding/medusa-vicuna-7b-v1.3` acceptance-rate test). It fails consistently (~4s, reproduced twice) with `RuntimeError: Engine core initialization failed... Failed core proc(s): {}` from `wait_for_engine_startup` -- before weight download or model loading begins. This looks like an engine-multiprocessing/sandbox limitation in the dev environment used for this PR, not something caused by this diff (the direct `from vllm.models.medusa import Medusa` import works, and the registry's own import-sanity test passes), but I haven't confirmed that against `main` yet. Flagging explicitly rather than claiming this test passes -- will confirm before marking ready for review.\n\n## Details\n\n**Convention followed:** matches already-migrated families (`deepseek_v32`, `kimi_k3`, `glm5next`, etc.) -- `vllm/models/<name>/__init__.py` re-exporting from `common/<name>.py`. Medusa is the first fully `common`-only package in the new layout (no existing family currently skips the `nvidia`/`amd` split entirely), since it has nothing hardware-specific to split out.\n\n**Duplicate-work check:** searched open issues/PRs (`gh issue list`/`gh pr list`, several keyword variants) before starting; found no PR doing this specific migration. One unrelated open PR (#48715, a large personal-fork rebase) happens to touch `medusa.py` incidentally among dozens of unrelated files -- not a competing Flat Model migration.\n\n**Scope:** this PR only moves Medusa. The other ~30 legacy drafter files (EAGLE/EAGLE3, MTP variants, DFlash) are out of scope here; most are entangled with their own not-yet-migrated base model and need to be scoped individually.\n\nThis PR is a draft while the e2e validation gap above is resolved.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI. (e2e acceptance-rate test not yet confirmed -- see Validation section)\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01S7agbtPNuVe9pxACkqbitP\n",
